e that may hinder crew cooperation. D offers strong responsibility and problem\u2011solving but lacks any evidence of calmness under pressure and may suffer from mood\u2011related crew issues.\n**Remaining uncertainty:** \u2013 How much B\u2019s pretentious, grumpy, or uncooperative demeanor actually impacts real\u2011world crew interaction on long flights. \u2013 Whether D\u2019s moodiness and loner tendency translate into unsafe or inefficient crew performance. \u2013 Absence of stress\u2011handling data for A and D leaves a gap in assessing their reliability under sustained pressure.\n**What would change my vote:** \u2013 Concrete evidence that B\u2019s communication style leads to significant crew friction or safety concerns would shift preference away from him. \u2013 Reliable data showing D can stay calm under extreme pressure and that his moodiness does not affect crew cooperation would make D a stronger contender. \u2013 Any positive stress\u2011handling or teamwork information for A would also raise his suitability.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}"}
